\section{Stress Testing and Stability Verification}
This section presents the full stress testing protocol and results obtained
from executing the Suprakernel Sovereign Architecture on a 64-node NVIDIA HGX
H100 cluster. The objective of the stress tests is to evaluate numerical
resilience, manifold stability, kernel mutation safety, and real-time
telemetry-driven enforcement of Lyapunov and CBF constraints under extreme
operational loads.

\subsection{Stress Testing Environment}
All experiments were conducted on a synchronized CUDA execution fabric
consisting of:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 64 HGX H100 nodes,
    \item 8$\times$H100 GPUs per node,
    \item NVLink 4.0 interconnect,
    \item RDMA-enabled MPI channels,
    \item direct-to-chip liquid cooling.
\end{itemize}
The cluster executed real-time ingestion, manifold projection, kernel mutation,
and stability verification at full operational capacity.

